# 0143 WIP: EP2 log frames 63 -> 511 bytes + rearm ring drain (USB branch).
# Two changes on top of 0142:
#   1. One log frame per GPD sized for the 512-byte MPS: 16 B header +
#      up to 495 B text = 511 bytes, one below wMaxPacketSize so every
#      GPD still ends on a short packet (QMU TX done requirement).
#      Slots are 512 B apart: no slot crosses a 16 KB page or a cache
#      line.  8x payload per frame vs the 0142 63-byte frames.
#   2. The reset/rearm path now calls ruby_ep2_ring_reset() after
#      stopping the TX QMU.  Measured on 0142: rearm zeroed
#      enq/deq/inflight while the ring still held 63 owned GPDs
#      (inflight=15 vs hwo=63) and stale frames were re-delivered in
#      later sessions.  The ring is reset while the QMU is stopped so
#      the counters match the hardware.
